## Phase 1 – Strengthen the no-mock gate (½ day)
- Extend `scripts/verify-no-mocks.ts` to fail on: `'Abebe'`, `MS0001`, `ETB` string literals in `apps/mobile`, `fallback`, `q-fallback`, and numeric literals assigned to price/days/percent props.
- Add the same scan to CI (`ci-test-and-lint.yml`).

## Phase 2 – Student identity & status from API (2–3 days)
- Add `GET /student/me/summary` returning: name, student code, account state, entitlement (expiry, days left), pending order count, per-course progress, continue-learning target.
- Mobile: replace the hardcoded Home props in `App.tsx` with this one hook (`useStudentSummary`), cached in SQLite for offline.
- Remove the `'Abebe Kebede'` initial state.

## Phase 3 – Pricing & store from `pricing_config` (2 days)
- All ETB amounts, course-count limits, tier discounts and the 180-day duration come from `GET /commerce/settings` / `quote`.
- Payment accounts (CBE, Telebirr, Abyssinia) already have admin CRUD (`/commerce/payment-methods`). The mobile checkout must render only that list.
- Admin: add a live "what the student sees" preview to the pricing page.

## Phase 4 – Quizzes, exams, questions fully from DB/MinIO (3 days)
- Delete fake chapter/question fallbacks. Show loading/empty/error states instead.
- Questions come from the course package stream (MinIO) or `/assessments/exam-sets/:id`, with SQLite cache.
- Admin builders are kept as they are (Mid / Final / Mock / COC tabs already exist).

## Phase 5 – Automatic sync when back online (3 days)
Current state: Home polls `delta` every 8 s, and `MobileSyncEngine` also exists. These two paths overlap.
- Make `MobileSyncEngine` the single path: triggers on app foreground, connection restored, and a ≥60 s timer while active (drop the 8 s poll to save battery/data).
- Use `catalog_tombstones` so admin deletions/unpublishes remove content from the device. Bump `version` on every admin change.
- Add content-package version check: if a downloaded course package is stale, re-download in the background (Wi-Fi only setting respected).
- Push `entitlement` changes (approval, refund, revoke) via the existing Expo push service plus next-sync fallback.
- Outbox: progress, attempts and profile edits flush on reconnect (only for registered students, per FR-A06).

## Phase 6 – Admin enhancements (keep existing UI/UX) (3–4 days)
- Home content controls: study-tip/announcement banner, featured course, quick-start card visibility (Daily Quiz, Exam Hall, Formula Sheets).
- Publish/unpublish and "pin as free sample" toggles on every content row.
- Sync status panel: per-student last sync time, app version, pending outbox size.
- Audit log entries for every publish/price/payment-account change.

## Phase 7 – Refactor (ongoing, after Phase 4 so behaviour is locked by tests)
- Split the giant files: `ProfileAndStoreScreens.tsx` (2,947 lines), `AssessmentsAndReviewScreens.tsx` (~1,800), `BeforeHomeAuthScreens.tsx`, and admin `questions/[examType]/new/page.tsx` (1,746) and `ScanToPdfWizard.tsx` (1,576).
